│ patch_description        │ Cross-over of the two programs: keep the direct constrained optimization (maximize min    │
│                          │ distance subject to diameter <= 1) from the SLSQP-based script, which achieved 0.98, but  │
│                          │ enrich the multistart initialization with the icosahedron-plus-perturbed-poles structured │
│                          │ start from the current program (a strong candidate configuration for 14 points). We run   │
│                          │ SLSQP from several starts (structured icosa, Fibonacci, and seeded random unit vectors),  │
│                          │ track the best dmin/dmax ratio, and fall back gracefully. The icosa start typically       │
│                          │ converges faster and to better local optima, while the random starts add diversity. Only  │
│                          │ a handful of starts are used to keep runtime well under the timeout (the reference took   │
│                          │ ~7s with 10 starts; we use 6 and tighter maxiter).                                        │
