│ patch_description        │ Replace the random point placement with a numerical optimizer. Since the metric is        │
│                          │ (dmin/dmax)^2, we can normalize scale each iteration so dmax=1 and run gradient ascent on │
│                          │ a soft-min of squared pairwise distances (log-sum-exp surrogate with annealing). We seed  │
│                          │ from several structured 14-point configurations (cube vertices + face centers, hexagonal  │
│                          │ prism + axis points, icosahedron + poles, random) and keep the best result over restarts, │
│                          │ making it deterministic via fixed seeds.                                                  │
