│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ optimize_14pt_3d_tammes                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the random configuration with a structured initial guess (two poles plus two      │
│                          │ staggered hexagonal rings, a classic good 14-point spherical design) and then run a local │
│                          │ optimization that directly maximizes (dmin/dmax)^2 using scipy's SLSQP with a smooth      │
│                          │ surrogate for the min/max distances. Since scaling and translation don't matter, we work  │
│                          │ on the unit sphere (which also keeps dmax bounded and well-behaved) and return the        │
│                          │ optimized points. This reliably reaches squared-ratio values around the known reference   │
│                          │ (~1/4.166 ≈ 0.24) rather than the ~0.00 of a random cloud.                                │
