│ patch_description        │ Return to the SLSQP constrained-optimization architecture (which reached 0.98), but       │
│                          │ restructure it: (1) a two-stage pipeline — stage 1 runs a cheap repulsion pre-optimizer   │
│                          │ to spread points apart and normalize diameter, stage 2 polishes with SLSQP maximizing     │
│                          │ dmin subject to dmax<=1; (2) diverse structured seeds (icosahedron+2 poles, Fibonacci     │
│                          │ sphere variants, random-on-sphere) instead of only random starts; (3) vectorized          │
│                          │ pair-distance computations and best-of-restarts selection on the true dmin/dmax ratio.    │
│                          │ The repulsion stage gives SLSQP a well-conditioned starting point so each restart         │
│                          │ converges reliably, improving score per unit time versus pure SLSQP from random starts.   │
