│ patch_name               │ two_phase_slsqp_repolish                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The previous pure-SLSQP version scored 0.98 while the current hybrid scored 0.93, so the  │
│                          │ repulsion stage's candidates may not feed SLSQP as good starting basins, and the SLSQP    │
│                          │ polish is under-converged. Improvements: (1) run SLSQP in a restart loop — after each     │
│                          │ converged run, re-run SLSQP starting from the previous solution with tighter ftol, which  │
│                          │ typically climbs out of the flat soft-min plateau near the optimum; (2) evaluate the true │
│                          │ ratio (dmin/dmax) for every polished result and keep the global best, including comparing │
│                          │ against the repulsion candidates themselves; (3) slightly increase repulsion iterations   │
│                          │ for better candidate quality. This adds moderate runtime but stays well below the timeout │
│                          │ (previous 7.36s version was acceptable).                                                  │
