│                          │ (beta=12) to escape poor basins, then re-polish with sharper beta=60 so the smooth        │
│                          │ min/max closely track the true discrete min/max; and (2) better initializers — the        │
│                          │ antipodal cube hint plus an icosahedron-derived seed (14 ≈ 12 icosahedron vertices + 2    │
│                          │ antipodal extras) are strong, well-spread starting basins for points on a sphere. A       │
│                          │ modest number of restarts (with a couple of random seeds) keeps runtime near a few        │
│                          │ seconds while the annealed polish sharpens the final ratio above the previous 0.93        │
│                          │ baseline.                                                                                 │
