│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_slsqp_diameter_refinement                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The previous SLSQP program (max dmin s.t. dmax ≤ 1) reached 0.98, while the current       │
│                          │ softmin/softmax pipeline only reaches 0.88. The soft-min/max surrogate smooths the        │
│                          │ objective and stalls away from the true ratio. Key insight: under the constraint dmax ≤   │
│                          │ 1, the ratio dmin/dmax equals exactly the minimized dmin, so the constrained problem      │
│                          │ directly optimizes the true metric. I add a SLSQP stage (maximize min distance subject to │
│                          │ max distance ≤ 1) applied to the top-ranked candidates from the cheap ranking pass, plus  │
│                          │ a final SLSQP polish of the best free-space point (after normalizing so dmax ≈ 1). This   │
│                          │ combines the good global search of the surrogate pipeline with the exact constrained      │
│                          │ optimizer that previously scored 0.98.                                                    │
