│ patch_name               │ antipodal_symmetry_polish                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The best-known configurations for 14 points (icosahedron + antipodal poles) are centrally │
│                          │ symmetric. After the SLSQP polishing loop, we add a final refinement pass: (1) attempt    │
│                          │ antipodal symmetrization — pair each point with its best-matching antipodal partner (via  │
│                          │ a greedy matching on -P), average each point with the negation of its partner to enforce  │
│                          │ exact central symmetry, (2) run a short, tight SLSQP polish (maxiter 200, ftol 1e-16)     │
│                          │ from the symmetrized configuration. Since the optimum is believed to be centrally         │
│                          │ symmetric, projecting onto the symmetric subspace and re-polishing can jump past local    │
│                          │ minima of the generic optimization and land on the (better) symmetric optimum. We keep    │
│                          │ the better of the original and symmetrized-polished results, so this can only improve the │
│                          │ outcome.                                                                                  │
