│                          │ gradient information everywhere, which typically pushes dmin noticeably higher under the  │
│                          │ same diameter constraint. I also add the recommended zero-cost safety checks              │
│                          │ (shape/finiteness assertions) so a malformed candidate cannot crash the whole run, and    │
│                          │ increase the number of internal restarts. Since the metric is squared-ratio, even a 1%    │
│                          │ gain in dmin/dmax is a ~2% score gain.                                                    │
