│ patch_description        │ The current pipeline already reaches ~0.98 of the reference squared ratio (1/4.1658). The │
│                          │ remaining gap is best closed by (a) broader multi-start coverage — adding two additional  │
│                          │ high-quality structured seeds (cuboctahedron-based, scaled icosahedron + equatorial pair) │
│                          │ and more random starts, and (b) polishing more of the top-ranked candidates with the      │
│                          │ exact constrained SLSQP solver (top 5 → top 8), since the SLSQP packing formulation is    │
│                          │ what converges to the true optimum basin. Additionally, I add cheap shape/finiteness      │
│                          │ assertions (per the recommendation) around the SLSQP and repulsion outputs so a malformed │
│                          │ candidate can never zero out the run, and a final "best-of" re-polish that re-runs SLSQP  │
│                          │ on the incumbent to squeeze out the last digits. These are low-cost, targeted changes     │
│                          │ that preserve the existing 19s runtime profile while nudging the ratio upward.            │
