│ patch_name               │ annealed_sphere_tammes                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ New approach: treat it as the Tammes/Best-packing problem in two phases. Phase 1: on the  │
│                          │ unit sphere, run annealed projected-gradient ascent on a log-sum-exp soft-minimum of      │
│                          │ pairwise distances (temperature geometrically cooled), which directly maximizes dmin with │
│                          │ dmax≤2 guaranteed by the sphere projection. This uses many diverse structured+random      │
│                          │ restarts. Phase 2: take the top candidates, release them from the sphere and refine with  │
│                          │ L-BFGS on a smooth (dmin/dmax)² surrogate with increasing sharpness beta, allowing dmax   │
│                          │ to shrink below 2 — the true objective can then exceed the spherical bound. Finally an    │
│                          │ exact-score swap/rotation micro-polish targets the bottleneck pair. True non-smooth score │
│                          │ is tracked throughout and the best configuration is returned.                             │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
