│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ icosahedron_poles_seed_and_early_exit                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The metric target ratio is (dmin/dmax)^2 ≈ 1/4.1658 ≈ 0.24003, achieved by the known      │
│                          │ optimal configuration for 14 points: an icosahedron's 12 vertices plus two antipodal      │
│                          │ points along an axis (poles), appropriately scaled. Random Gaussian seeds rarely converge │
│                          │ to this. I add explicit structured seeds (icosahedron + poles variants with varying pole  │
│                          │ radius and rotations), keep a couple of random seeds, optimize each with L-BFGS-B on the  │
│                          │ smooth min/max objective, and exit early once the target ratio ~0.2395 is reached (score  │
│                          │ ≥ that means combined_score ≥ 0.997). This both boosts score and controls runtime.        │
