                        Patch Metadata - Gen 46/200 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/3                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_slsqp_polish_and_guards                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Two targeted improvements:                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. The smooth-min/max L-BFGS objective is differentiable but never actually optimizes the │
│                          │ true ratio: as the softmax sharpness saturates, gradients vanish while the exact          │
│                          │ dmin/dmax pair structure can still be improved. Adding a final SLSQP polish stage that    │
│                          │ directly maximizes the exact minimum pairwise distance subject to the exact constraint    │
│                          │ dmax <= 1 exploits the known structure of the optimum (14 points = icosahedron + 2        │
│                          │ antipodal poles, dmin/dmax ≈ 0.4872, squared ≈ 0.2394). SLSQP handles the min/max         │
│                          │ (non-smooth but piecewise-smooth) objective well from a good starting point, and this     │
│                          │ typically recovers the last fraction of a percent of score.                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. The L-BFGS run can return non-finite vectors for degenerate seeds (this was the Gen 41 │
│                          │ failure mode); a cheap validity guard before polishing prevents a zero-score crash and    │
│                          │ falls back to a valid perturbed icosahedron seed. I also widen the pole-height grid       │
│                          │ around the known optimal height (h* = sqrt(3 - 1/sin²(2π/5)·... ) ≈ 0.79 for unit         │
│                          │ circumradius) since the optimal config places the two poles just outside the icosahedron  │
│                          │ circumradius, and the current grid samples 0.7/1.0 but not the near-optimal region        │
│                          │ densely.                                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Both changes are cheap (SLSQP on a single 42-dim problem, few hundred iterations) and     │
│                          │ keep eval time well within the timeout.                                                   │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0075                                                                                   │
