│ patch_name               │ smooth_jac_cascade_anneal                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current program already reaches the reference ratio, so the new design focuses on     │
│                          │ squeezing the last digits out via a fundamentally better optimizer core: (1) SLSQP now    │
│                          │ receives analytic Jacobians for both the soft-min objective and all 91 pairwise diameter  │
│                          │ constraints (as a single vector-valued constraint), which makes the nonsmooth "max        │
│                          │ diameter" boundary tractable and convergence far more reliable; (2) an escalating-ftol    │
│                          │ perturbation cascade (1e-12 → 1e-14 with tiny Gaussian restarts, keep-the-better) attacks │
│                          │ borderline plateaus exactly where score is won or lost; (3) a richer, cheaper seed zoo    │
│                          │ (antiprisms with varying twist/height, icosahedron+poles, two-shell, Fibonacci, random    │
│                          │ spheres) feeds a repulsion pre-stage that normalizes diameter and soft-maximizes all      │
│                          │ distances via inverse-power forces, so SLSQP starts near the constraint boundary.         │
│                          │ Everything is deterministic (seeded RNG) and returns a validated (14,3) array.            │
