│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ hard_constraint_slsqlp_polish                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The softmin/softmax surrogate in `_neg_obj` only approaches the true objective as beta→∞, │
│                          │ so L-BFGS-B converges to borderline plateaus just below the true optimum (min_max_ratio   │
│                          │ 0.21 vs the ~0.24 reference). The decisive improvement is to add a hard-constrained SLSQP │
│                          │ stage that directly maximizes t subject to d_ij² ≥ t and d_ij² ≤ 1 (all pairwise          │
│                          │ distances simultaneously bounded, which is *exactly* the min-max ratio problem). SLSQP    │
│                          │ handles analytic constraint Jacobians, so this is cheap for 14 points (91 pairs, 43       │
│                          │ variables). We then apply escalating-tolerance passes with small perturbation restarts    │
│                          │ (as recommended), always keeping the better configuration, so every pass is risk-free.    │
