│ patch_name               │ early_exit_target_ratio                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The reference squared ratio is 1/4.165849767, i.e. a linear min/max ratio of              │
│                          │ sqrt(1/4.165849767) ≈ 0.49006. Once any candidate reaches this ratio, further polishing   │
│                          │ of the same seed (and the "init" duplicate candidate) cannot improve the final score      │
│                          │ meaningfully — it just burns time and risks SLSQP drifting slightly. This edit adds a     │
│                          │ TARGET_RATIO constant and early exits: (1) inside the seed loop, skip the raw "init"      │
│                          │ candidate if the repulsion-pre-then-SLSQP candidate already meets the target; (2) after   │
│                          │ the repulsion stage, check the ratio directly and skip SLSQP entirely if the target is    │
│                          │ already met; (3) stop the multi-pass polish loop once the target is reached. This         │
│                          │ preserves score (the achieved ratio ~0.49 matches the reference) while reducing eval      │
│                          │ time, and keeps behavior deterministic.                                                   │
