│ patch_name               │ antipodal_beam_pipeline                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Structural redesign around an explicit candidate-pipeline architecture. Instead of the    │
│                          │ previous monolithic staged search, the program is organized as a pipeline of independent  │
│                          │ refinement operators (sanitize/normalize, sphere soft-opt, exact SLSQP packing with       │
│                          │ pre/post validation, and a new antipodal 7-pair reparameterization that halves the search │
│                          │ space and enforces central symmetry). A beam of candidates flows through the pipeline,    │
│                          │ with each operator returning a validated (points, score) result; the driver simply        │
│                          │ composes operators and keeps the global incumbent. The antipodal stage exploits the fact  │
│                          │ that optimal 14-point packings tend toward antipodal symmetry, giving a much smaller,     │
│                          │ better-conditioned optimization problem that can push the ratio above the reference       │
│                          │ value. Robustness guards (shape/finite checks before any optimizer call) are centralized  │
│                          │ in the sanitize operator.                                                                 │
